    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). There's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, and its `coreComposesSalutation` case is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature so the app composes `title + ' ' + lastName` (or just `lastName` when no title is given).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only, derived `salutation` field to the `Owner` schema. (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, so `OwnerFieldsDto.title` and `OwnerDto.salutation` get generated automatically.)\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `title` column (getter/setter) and a `@Transient getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema is authoritative).\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 The seed rows use positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I injected a `NULL` for the new `title` column into all 10 rows. The h2/mysql/postgres data files use named-column inserts and needed no change.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` required no edits \u2014 `title` (input) and `salutation` (output) map by matching property name automatically.",
